From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Subject: [PATCH] t880: allocate decode presentation buffers through Panthor DRM

T880 copies decoded NV12 into stable GPU presentation storage. Allocate that
storage through the Panthor render node and export a PRIME fd, rather than
requiring DMA-heap device access from sandboxed VA-API consumers. Preserve
CPU-access synchronization, reservation-fence waits and previously exported
storage identities. Keep system DMA heaps for new upload/write allocations
and the noncoherent VPU input path.

